version 2.15.4 (last update 2026-11-21)
        + Add the function ancombc3 (ANCOM-BC3): differential abundance,
          differential prevalence, and omnibus tests under a zero-inflated
          Poisson-log-normal model, with the global test, pairwise
          comparisons, the Dunnett's type of test, the trend test, and
          repeated measures; ancombc3 requires the package torch, which is
          listed in Suggests
        + Add ancombc3_default_settings, plot_ancombc3_training, and the
          print and summary methods for the result of ancombc3
        + Add compiled code (src) for the second stage of ancombc3
        + Add the vignette ANCOM-BC3 Tutorial

version 2.15.3 (last update 2026-11-21)
        + Preserve single-column metadata (PR #343 by @hyperpolymath)
        + Align mixed-model degrees of freedom by coefficient name (PR #342
          by @xec-cm)
        + Assign a screening p-value of 1 in the Dunnett's type of test to
          taxa whose mixed model cannot be fitted (#321, #340, #266)
        + Fix the 'subscript out of bounds' error in ancombc2 with
          rand_formula when the mixed model cannot be built for the last
          pattern of missing values
        + Make the mixed-model check before the random-effects fit
          independent of the order of the taxa (#294, #271, #323)
        + Fix the random-effects global test, and the pairwise test that uses
          it, when the group variable is the first or only term of
          fix_formula (#262, #210, #312)
        + Fix the errors in messages that list many names or names containing
          '%' (#243)
        + Apply the aliases rank and assay.type in ancom, ancombc, ancombc2,
          secom_linear, and secom_dist (#319)
        + Use the same samples for the original and the aggregated tables in
          secom_linear and secom_dist (#316)
        + Stop with an informative error when no fixed effect can be
          estimated from the nonzero samples of any taxon (#257)
        + Stop the cluster when a parallel run ends with an error
        + Stop with a clear message when a multi-group test is requested and
          the group variable is not in the formula (#308)
        + Exclude taxa with zero first-stage variances from the bias
          estimation instead of stopping, and document the order in which
          prv_cut and lib_cut are applied (#309, #325)
        + Report a coefficient that is not estimable for a taxon as NA
          instead of 0, so that it does not enter the pairwise, Dunnett's
          type, or trend tests (#298)

version 2.15.xx (last update 2026-09-18)
        + Reduce the running time of ancombc, ancombc2, secom_linear, and
          secom_dist without changing the results
        + Add the 'conservative' argument to ancombc2, which specifies whether
          the pseudo-counts of the sensitivity analysis are added before or
          after the estimation of sampling fractions
        + Fix the error in ancombc2 when the trend test is requested with the
          sensitivity analysis but without the global test
        + Correct documented defaults and return values in the help pages and
          README
        + Add the help topic ANCOMBC-concepts, which defines structural zeros
          and the mixed directional false discovery rate once for all functions

version 2.12.xx (last update 2026-04-27)
        + Remove CVXR dependences

